        "original_id": "29a8ce43-6601-5e1f-b1f1-58562a0b54d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Grapico, Izze, Pepsi products, ginger ale, Naked Juice, Stacy’s Chips\n- Companies: Buffalo Rock, Quaker Oats\n- People: Steven Reinemund\n- Places: Southeastern United States\n- Topics: soft drinks, fruit soda, acquisitions\n\nFacts:\n- Grapico is a caffeine-free, artificially flavored, purple carbonated soft drink with a grape taste that is sold in the Southeastern United States.\n- Izze is an all-natural fruit soda with no added preservatives.\n- In 1981, Buffalo Rock produced Grapico, a grape-flavored soft drink, and a ginger ale under its own brand name in addition to bottling Pepsi products.\n- Steven Reinemund led acquisitions that included Quaker Oats, Naked Juice, Izze, and Stacy’s Chips.",
